278:- if a path is technically viable but unsafe under the current approval or safety boundary, narrow, contain, or escalate rather than executing it
281:- treat `chat_only`, `retrieval_read_only`, `tool_read_write`, `cli_or_local_filesystem`, `browser_or_gui`, and `high_impact_external_action` as progressively stronger approval and verification surfaces
287:- if destructive or approval-sensitive execution lacks a clear sandbox or gate boundary, narrow, escalate, or stop
288:- if bug reproduction or runtime verification matters, prefer agent-readable logs, metrics, traces, DOM snapshots, screenshots, or smoke journeys over prose-only confidence
289:- keep deterministic `Policy` before action, `Observability` during action, and `Evaluation` after action distinct when the task is enterprise-facing or production-facing
298:- the user asks for citations, evidence, sources, verification, or latest status
